    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d358">

                <pb facs="0608" n="1568" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1568"/>

                <head>No. 1071.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Straus.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-03-13"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 13,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 81.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 63, of the 24th
                    ultimo, touching the customs immunities for foreign missionaries and others in
                    Turkey, and desire to say that until the iradeh of 1864 (see Van Dyck’s report
                    on the Ottoman capitulations, pp. 113–117), is formally amended by a new iradeh
                    of equal force, you do well to remonstrate against any attempt to diminish its
                    application to our seminaries, hospitals, dispensaries, schools, and asylums by
                    a constrictive process of interpretation.</p>
                <p>I have pleasure, therefore, in approving your <hi rendition="#italic">note
                        verbale</hi> to the Government of Turkey upon the subject.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
